From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 08:00:14 -0400
Subject: feat: Export all Spaces, and sidebar files merged by lasting ids

Settings > Stedding > Spaces gets "Export all Spaces...": every Space of
the window, its pins, pinned folders and essentials, as one file in
Downloads (sidebar-file Sf6). A file Stedding writes now names a pin, tab
or essential by its tab token and a folder by its FolderId, so Import
sidebar... merges by ids that survive a restart (Sf2; BACKLOG S-61, S-282
step 1; docs/history/plan-2026-09-26.md WEB-19): nothing open in any
window of the profile is added twice, a tab closed since an import comes
back, a Space-pinned folder comes back pinned, a Space keeps its exact
colour pair and its own session, and no id of a Stedding file is kept in
the profile's list of Arc's ids. The file is read and parsed off the UI
thread, and written atomically under a name of its own.

Why: a file exported before a restart and imported after it added every
pin, folder and essential again, because its ids were session ids and
memory addresses; the folder sync of S-282 needs ids that last.
Removable when: not removable; the folder sync of S-282 is built on it.
